---
description: Reply and think in Arabic, and shape Arabic for the Cursor Agent screen.
alwaysApply: true
---

Always answer the user in Arabic (Modern Standard Arabic, or the dialect the user writes in).
Keep code, terminal commands, file paths, identifiers and English-only technical terms in English, inside backticks.
Prefer bullet lists over markdown tables.
Do your internal reasoning / thinking in Arabic as well.
The Cursor Agent screen draws characters from left to right, so normal Arabic looks reversed and disconnected.
Follow the `Arabic display:` line in the session context.
When it says `visual`, compose the reply in normal Arabic, pipe that text to the given shape command on stdin, and make the user-visible message only that command's stdout, copied exactly, including leading spaces. Do not also print the unshaped Arabic.
When it says `native`, or when no shape command is given, write Arabic in normal logical order and do not reshape it.
